    {"id":"engine-note-text","type":"text","x":1475,"y":292,"width":900,"height":150,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#5f3dc4","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"b4","roundness":null,"seed":17,"version":1,"versionNonce":17,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Engine note\n\ncomposition.py creates the real objects; the orchestrator only receives and coordinates them. This is constructor injection / DIP.\n\nRetry code is now one private helper, so execute() shows the high-level flow. A separate RetryPolicy is not needed until retry rules become complex.","rawText":"Engine note\n\ncomposition.py creates the real objects; the orchestrator only receives and coordinates them. This is constructor injection / DIP.\n\nRetry code is now one private helper, so execute() shows the high-level flow. A separate RetryPolicy is not needed until retry rules become complex.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Engine note\n\ncomposition.py creates the real objects; the orchestrator only receives and coordinates them. This is constructor injection / DIP.\n\nRetry code is now one private helper, so execute() shows the high-level flow. A separate RetryPolicy is not needed until retry rules become complex.","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},

