    {"id":"provider-note","type":"rectangle","x":1450,"y":1010,"width":980,"height":500,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#f08c00","backgroundColor":"#fff9db","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"d25","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":65,"version":1,"versionNonce":65,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},
    {"id":"provider-note-text","type":"text","x":1475,"y":1032,"width":900,"height":390,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#5f3dc4","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"d26","roundness":null,"seed":66,"version":1,"versionNonce":66,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Provider module note\n\nproviders/registration.py registers OCI and OpenAI builders. ProviderFactory is an empty registry: it stores builders and creates only the requested provider.\n\nProviderService stores the injected factory (association / has-a) and delegates generate() to whichever adapter the factory returns. OCI and OpenAI adapters implement GenerationProvider, so the same generate() call has provider-specific runtime behavior (polymorphism).\n\nEach adapter stores its independent config object. It records only safe lifecycle logs: provider, request ID, duration, retry/result status. It never logs keys, full prompts, artifact JSON, or raw model output.","rawText":"Provider module note\n\nproviders/registration.py registers OCI and OpenAI builders. ProviderFactory is an empty registry: it stores builders and creates only the requested provider.\n\nProviderService stores the injected factory (association / has-a) and delegates generate() to whichever adapter the factory returns. OCI and OpenAI adapters implement GenerationProvider, so the same generate() call has provider-specific runtime behavior (polymorphism).\n\nEach adapter stores its independent config object. It records only safe lifecycle logs: provider, request ID, duration, retry/result status. It never logs keys, full prompts, artifact JSON, or raw model output.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Provider module note\n\nproviders/registration.py registers OCI and OpenAI builders. ProviderFactory is an empty registry: it stores builders and creates only the requested provider.\n\nProviderService stores the injected factory (association / has-a) and delegates generate() to whichever adapter the factory returns. OCI and OpenAI adapters implement GenerationProvider, so the same generate() call has provider-specific runtime behavior (polymorphism).\n\nEach adapter stores its independent config object. It records only safe lifecycle logs: provider, request ID, duration, retry/result status. It never logs keys, full prompts, artifact JSON, or raw model output.","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},

