    {"id":"result-note","type":"rectangle","x":1450,"y":1870,"width":980,"height":300,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#f08c00","backgroundColor":"#fff9db","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"f15","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":97,"version":1,"versionNonce":97,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},
    {"id":"result-note-text","type":"text","x":1475,"y":1892,"width":900,"height":230,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#5f3dc4","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"f16","roundness":null,"seed":98,"version":1,"versionNonce":98,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Validation, response and error note\n\nJsonResponseValidator returns JsonValidationResult. The orchestrator reads it and creates the final ExecutionResponse.\n\nInvalid model output causes a repair retry. Invalid user input and other domain errors are not retried; main.run() catches StructuredOutputError and returns a safe error response.\n\nSpecialized domain errors inherit StructuredOutputError, so the outer boundary can handle them consistently.","rawText":"Validation, response and error note\n\nJsonResponseValidator returns JsonValidationResult. The orchestrator reads it and creates the final ExecutionResponse.\n\nInvalid model output causes a repair retry. Invalid user input and other domain errors are not retried; main.run() catches StructuredOutputError and returns a safe error response.\n\nSpecialized domain errors inherit StructuredOutputError, so the outer boundary can handle them consistently.","fontSize":18,"fontFamily":5,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"Validation, response and error note\n\nJsonResponseValidator returns JsonValidationResult. The orchestrator reads it and creates the final ExecutionResponse.\n\nInvalid model output causes a repair retry. Invalid user input and other domain errors are not retried; main.run() catches StructuredOutputError and returns a safe error response.\n\nSpecialized domain errors inherit StructuredOutputError, so the outer boundary can handle them consistently.","autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25},

    {"id":"memory-panel","type":"rectangle","x":40,"y":2220,"width":2390,"height":600,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1971c2","backgroundColor":"#f8f9fa","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"index":"g0","roundness":{"type":3},"seed":99,"version":1,"versionNonce":99,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":null,"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},
